1. Input Collection Layer
Goal: Gather all required financial and contextual data.
Inputs:
  Financial statements (Income Statement, Balance Sheet, Cash Flow)
  Market data (stock prices, industry benchmarks)
  User query (e.g., “Analyze Apple’s financial performance”)
  Time period (quarterly, yearly)
Agent Tasks:
  Validate input format
  Normalize data (currency, dates)
  Handle missing values

2. Data Processing Agent
Goal: Clean and structure raw data.
Steps:
  Remove inconsistencies
  Convert to structured format (e.g., pandas DataFrame)
  Standardize metrics (e.g., revenue, EBITDA)
Output:
  Clean financial dataset ready for analysis

3. Financial Metrics Computation Agent
Goal: Calculate key financial indicators.
Key Metrics:
  Profitability:
    Net Profit Margin
    Gross Margin
    ROE, ROA
  Liquidity:
    Current Ratio
    Quick Ratio
  Leverage:
    Debt-to-Equity Ratio
  Efficiency:
    Asset Turnover

4. Trend Analysis Agent
Goal: Identify patterns over time.
Tasks:
  Year-over-year (YoY) growth
  Quarter-over-quarter (QoQ) trends
  Detect anomalies or sudden changes
Optional:
  Time-series forecasting

5. Benchmarking Agent
Goal: Compare against industry or competitors.
Tasks:
  Compare metrics with:
  Industry averages
  Key competitors
  Rank performance

6. Insight Generation Agent (LLM-powered)
Goal: Turn numbers into meaningful insights.
Examples:
  “Revenue grew 12% YoY driven by increased demand…”
  “Declining margins indicate rising operational costs…”

7. Risk Assessment Agent
Goal: Identify financial risks.
Checks:
  High debt levels
  Declining cash flow
  Volatility in earnings
  Market risks

8. Report Generation Agent
Goal: Produce a structured, human-readable report.
Sections:
  Executive Summary
  Financial Overview
  Key Metrics
  Trend Analysis
  Benchmark Comparison
  Risks & Opportunities
  Conclusion
Formats:
  PDF
  HTML dashboard
  Markdown / text

9. Visualization Agent (Optional)
Goal: Enhance understanding with visuals.
Charts:
  Revenue trends (line chart)
  Profit margins (bar chart)
  Ratio comparisons

10. Output Delivery Agent
Goal: Deliver the report.
Options:
  Downloadable file
  Web dashboard
  API response

Implementation Stack
  Data Processing: pandas, NumPy
  LLM Models: Hugging Face (t5-small, flan-t5, etc.)
  Pipelines: transformers pipeline API
  Visualization: matplotlib / Plotly
  Backend: Python (Flask / FastAPI)
  UI (Optional): Qt (fits your current C++ GUI work)
